course: dictionary
lesson: 3405
title: Explicit: clear, or openly for adults
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Explicit has two meanings. The first is clear and full: «explicit instructions» tell you exactly what to do, leaving nothing to guess. The second is about showing things very openly, and it is not suitable for children.
explain: The words around it tell you which meaning fits. In a classroom, «explicit instructions» are clear steps. On a song or film, the label «explicit» is a warning. Look for clues such as adult themes or a warning label.
explain: «An "E" next to a song means explicit, usually swearing or adult themes; many songs have a clean version.» So an E is a warning that the song is for adults. A clean version has the same song without the rude words. If you see an E, tell an adult and choose the clean version.
fact: «Explicit» is an adjective, and its adverb is «explicitly».
fact: «Explicit» can mean said clearly and fully, so nobody can be confused.
fact: «Explicit» can also mean showing things very openly, especially violence or sex, which is not suitable for children.
fact: In maths, an «explicit formula» gives the answer directly.
fact: If you see an explicit label, do not watch or listen; tell an adult.
exercise: «The teacher gave explicit instructions for the science test.» What does explicit mean here? | *Clear and full, so nobody is confused | Very loud and noisy | Hidden and secret | Late and rushed
exercise: A letter «E» next to a song warns you of what? | The tune is very slow | It is a party song | The song was made in a studio | *Swearing or adult themes, not suitable for children
exercise: In maths, an explicit formula does what? | Hides the answer | Asks a question | *Gives the answer directly | Makes a picture
test: Mum says a film has an explicit label. What should you do? | Turn the volume up | *Tell an adult and do not watch it | Watch it quickly before anyone sees | Share it with your friends
test: What is the adverb form of explicit? | explicit | explicitness | *explicitly | explicitful
exam: The teacher said, «Write your answer explicitly.» What does she want? | Vague answers that are only guessed | Answers drawn as pictures | Answers written in code | *Clear answers with everything stated fully
